  "physics_note": "v2 used vx=2, vy0=0 (near-vertical horizontal-launch drop; visually read as a weak, unresolved fall). v3 adds an initial upward vy0=10 m/s and raises vx to 15 m/s, giving a standard ballistic (thrown-at-an-angle) parabola: x(t)=x0+vx*t, y(t)=y0+vy0*t-0.5*g*t^2. Verified in-bounds (world x in (-95,95), y in (5,195) with r=5 margin) for all 40 scenes at both g=9.8 and g=4.9 across all 151 frames. x0 grid spacing changed from 20m to 10m (range -70..0 instead of -70..70) to keep the wider horizontal travel (75m over 5s, up from 10m) inside the world."
